course: dictionary
lesson: 7242
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Picket is one of them. To find the right meaning, look at the words around it, as you would with any new word. Ask yourself which meaning fits the sentence.
explain: A picket can be a pointed wooden stake in a fence, as in «a picket fence». In the USA, a «white picket fence» stands for a neat family home, so the words around it can give the picket a meaning beyond the fence itself.
explain: At work, a picket line is a group of striking workers standing outside their workplace with signs, peacefully asking others not to go in. «Don't cross the picket line.» Here, picket is a noun about people.
explain: «There are also ways workers stand up for themselves: unions, strikes, picket lines and tribunals.» Picket can also be a verb: to picket means to stand outside a place to protest. Try your meaning in the sentence; if it still makes sense, you have found it.
fact: A picket is a pointed wooden stake, often part of a fence.
fact: A «picket line» is a group of striking workers standing outside their workplace to protest.
fact: To picket means to stand outside a place to protest.
fact: In old army stories, a picket was a small group of soldiers on guard.
fact: A «white picket fence» often stands for a neat, happy family home, especially in the USA.
exercise: «The garden had a white picket fence all around it.» What is a picket here? | A kind of garden tool for digging | A small group of soldiers on guard | *A pointed wooden stake, used in a fence | A group of workers on strike
exercise: «The workers stood on the picket line outside the factory.» What does picket line mean? | A row of plants in the garden | A list of names for a school trip | A line of cars waiting at the traffic lights | *A group of striking workers standing outside their workplace to protest
exercise: «The workers will picket the factory gates.» What does picket mean in this sentence? | To sleep inside the factory | To build a new fence | *To stand outside a place to protest | To paint the gates bright blue
test: In old army stories, what is a picket? | A kind of cannon | *A small group of soldiers on guard | A map of the battle | A horse with a long tail
test: «Don't cross the picket line.» What does this ask you to do? | *Not to go past the strikers and into the workplace | Run faster than the others | Jump over the fence | Buy a ticket first
exam: The strikers stood on the picket line and asked others not to go in. Why did they stand there? | To sell ice cream to passers-by | To sleep outside after a long day | *To peacefully ask others not to go in | To build a fence around the factory
